hey guys it's Jonah here so imagine this  you just had a really solid workout  session and you feel satisfied with how  much you have pushed yourself so you go  to bed and the next morning when you try  to get up oh my god your leg muscles are  so sore you can barely walk so you'd sit  there struggling to get by the next few  days and you can't even get back into  your fitness routine what you're  experiencing is called  delay onset muscle soreness also known  as Dom's Dom's is caused by microscopic  tearing of the muscle fibers that are  then repaired as part of the muscle  growth process the soreness is felt most  strongly between 24 to 72 hours after  exercising Dom's is extremely common  especially if you're new to exercising  if you change your workout routine or if  you dramatically increase the intensity  and duration of your exercise so  beginners there is nothing to worry  about  post-workout muscle soreness is part of  muscle adaptation and muscle development  it is something anyone and everyone who  has ever worked out can relate to so the  most common question is can I avoid  Dom's  altogether what to simply put the answer  is known but there are steps which you  can take to reduce and prevent Dom's and  also to help your muscles recover  quicker so the first tip is stretch at  the end of your workouts well there has  been a lot of debate in regards to  whether or not stretching at the end of  your workout will help to reduce muscle  soreness when you train you contract the  muscles as a result the muscle fibers  will get shorter and tighten up when you  stretch it will help to lengthen the  muscles it will relieve the feeling of  tightness and promote the better muscle  recovery if however you find yourself  disagreeing - this will just put it this  way stretching also helps with  flexibility and we want that so there is  no harm to include a quick 10 to 15  minutes of stretching after a good solid  workout the second tip is to soak in a  warm bath warm water can increase blood  flow and help loosen up tight or sore  muscles but do not jump into the hot tub  immediately after your workouts when  your body heat is already high and your  muscles are breaking down soaking in a  hot tub immediately will only further  damage your muscles so take a warm bath  once you have cooled down and your body  has written to its resting temperature  if your pen is isolated what you can do  is to apply direct hit to the spot by  using peel and stick on heat pads the  next tip is to massage your sore spots  so getting a message isn't just about  pampering yourself it can help to  promote blood flow and to ease tight  muscles so it can help to speed up  muscle recovery so if you can go for a  light and gentle massage not the rough  kind okay rough massages can sometimes  only further injure your muscles  remember that messages should somewhat  be relaxing and you shouldn't be in  constant pain if however you can't get  messages then invest in a foam roller  the foam roller works similar to massage  by increasing blood flow to your muscles  and the best part is it is cheap easy to  use and you can do it on your own foam  rolling involves a technique called  self myofascial release which uses  pressure and targets of the connective  tissue covering the muscles so put the  roller on the floor use your body weight  to apply pressure and roll back and  forth over the soil areas for about one  minute if this is your first time doing  it just take it easy and eventually you  will get the hang of it remember before  doing that check that your rehydrated  and that your heart rate is back to  normal when your muscles are hot and  loaded with lattic acid you can only  make it worse the next tip is to pack on  omega-3s when your muscles are sore your  muscles are basically inflamed omega-3s  are known to help reduce inflammation so  pack on food which are rich in omega  threes such as salmon oily fish chia  seeds flax seeds avocado spinach walnut  or edamame or for convenience you can  even take fish oil pills on a daily  basis and another very important tip is  to get plenty of rest as much as you  want to push yourself in your workouts  getting plenty of rest is just as  important that means getting al  is six to eight hours of sleep every  night and giving yourself at least one  full rest day a week when you don't get  enough rest it will not only affect your  fitness performance but your muscles  will also recover slower so prioritize  your sleep as much as you prioritize  your workouts and the final tip is move  it when your muscles are so sorry you  can barely walk or even get out of bed  you are more inclined just to sit on the  couch and pray that the pain will go  away well that is the last thing you  should be doing just know this  circulation promotes healing and if  you're just set on the couch doing  absolutely nothing the blood in your  body will not be able to flow hence you  will not recover what you should be  doing is to continue your workout  through active recovery it is basically  low intensity exercises just to get the  blood in your body flowing without  texting the muscles so think of gentle  yoga classes brisk walking an easy hike  or even a relaxing swim you can do this  the next day after an intense session or  even for a couple more days if your  muscles are extremely sore so guys my  recommendation is to alternate your  workout intensity so for instance  alternate between two days of high  intensity with two days of moderate  intensity and two days of low intensity  this will ensure that you are getting  the best result through your workouts  and that your body is still getting  plenty of time to recover and remember  when you experience post workout muscle  soreness the goal is to increase blood  flow into your muscles and to relieve  the feeling of tightness wanting to  achieve great fitness result isn't just  about the training aspect it includes  eating well and getting plenty of rest  when you're able to find that balance  not only will you be able to train  stronger for longer you will also see  results in the most efficient way if you  find this video to be helpful be sure to  like it and share it as well all the  best  you
 

